on with <italic>Le. infantum</italic>.  These presentations vary from (a) no clinical signs and robust healthy behavior in a young healthy Foxhound to (b) multiple clinical signs (polysymptomatic) including poor hair coat, enlarged liver and spleen, and crusty cutaneous lesions seen on the rump in an older hound.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="IPID2009-802712.001"/></fig></floats-wrap></article>